 cliques’ first vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"coreNumbers().degeneracyOrdering","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", then as Bron–Kerbosch with Tomita’s pivot (ties to the least","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"index) and branches in ascending index meets them. The sequence holds the graph, so iterating","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again gives the same cliques. O(n + m) before the first clique, O(d·n·3^(d\/3)) in all for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"degeneracy d.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MaximalCliques","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cliques\/documentation\/Cliques\/MaximalCliques","url":"\/documentation\/cliques\/maximalcliques"}}}